KNOWNBUG
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ four levels: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The bound (same_template_depth >= 3) is a heuristic: raising it to 4 makes
this pass but cpp17_headers1 ten times slower.  A guard that detects actual
recursion (repeated or growing template arguments) instead of counting
instances would fix both.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
